r the Degni-Drisko property was verified at these lengths by two independently written programs.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBalanced problems on graphs with categorization of edges (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268866169_Balanced_problems_on_graphs_with_categorization_of_edges)\nciteturn1search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; We also show that when the cost matrix is specially structured, QBOP can be solved as a sequence of linear balanced optimization problems. ... We study two generalizations of balanced optimization problems on graphs based on a partition of edges of a graph into categories and show that both are NP-complete for the path, perfect matching, spanning tree problem and for the travelling salesman problem on halin graphs.\n\nColour–balanced Networks\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Emília Draženská\n  * Jozef Kondáš\n  * Štefan Schrötter\n\nThis paper is a specific application of the combinatorial optimization methods for a problem in occuring in practice. We have created a mathematical model which describes clearly and in details real mathematical situation.\n\nView\n\n\nOptimization problems on graphs with categorizatio of edges\n\nArticle\n\n  * Štefan Berežný\n  * Katarína Cechlárová\n  * Vladimír Lacko\n\nWe study two generalizations of balanced optimization problems on graphs based on a partition of edges of a graph into categories and show that both are NP-complete for the path, perfect matching, spanning tree problem and for the travelling salesman problem on halin graphs.\n\nA polynomially solvable case of optimization problems on graphs with categorization of edges\n\n  * Jan 1999\n  * 25-31\n\n  * Š Berežný\n  * K Cechlárová\n  * V Lacko\n\nŠ. Berežný, K. Cechlárová and V. Lacko, A polynomially solvable case of optimization problems on graphs with categorization of edges, in: Proc. of MME'1999 (Jindřichúv Hradec, 1999) 25-31.\n\n---------------------------